# Python bytecode caches are generated, never committed
__pycache__/
# the local virtual environment folder
.venv/
# a local Python install folder some setups create in the repo
Python/
# scratch output folder for test evidence, not tracked
test_evidence_files/
# Generated by `python -m ddi_backend.load_data load` (rebuild any time)
# (the SQLite database built from DDI_Database.json and hp.json)
medications.db
# Mutable state written by the guarded agent and retrieval cache
# (review queue, request log and cached embeddings: the only writable file)
agent_state.db
# older/alternate name for the state file, also ignored
app_state.db
# cached embedding vectors from the optional embedding tier
*.embeddings.npz
# offline knowledge-graph export from scripts/export_graph.py
data/graph_export/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FILE SUMMARY: Tells git which generated, local or mutable files to leave out of the repository: bytecode caches,
# the virtual environment, the built database, the agent state file and cached embeddings, and the graph export.
# test_hygiene.py checks that medications.db, agent_state.db and .venv are listed here.
# (git only allows comments on their own line, so every note sits above the pattern it describes.)
# ASSIGNMENT TOOL: supporting infrastructure (not one of the assignment tools); it keeps the generated artefacts of the
# knowledge graph database, guarded agent state and embedding cache out of version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
